    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d289">

                <pb facs="0340" n="264" xml:id="pg264"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 422.11G93/834</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Hartman to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Quito</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-24">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 24, 1916</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my cable of January 11, 4 p.m. Negotiations for private settlement,
                    resumed Saturday, resulted in agreement on tariff and various matters connected
                    with railway administration. Other questions postponed until return of Mr.
                    Norton who leaves for United States to-morrow. Situation encouraging.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
